Call a capability from your shell, host a peer, inspect a live session in the
REPL, or expose CapTP tools over MCP. The command uses the same Host and
transport implementations as the library. Complete command and configuration
reference:
[docs/cli.md](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/docs/cli.md).

```sh
zig build
export PATH="$PWD/zig-out/bin:$PATH"
pancake help
```

# Encrypted conversation

Native rooms traffic rides [iroh]($link.page('transports/iroh')):

```sh
pancake app rooms-peer
```

# Lab round-trip

`ocapn listen` binds loopback `tcp`, the testing transport: a cleartext
`host:port` with no identity proof.

The CLI's demo greeter accepts the verb `greet` and one argument, then returns
`Hello, <arg>`.
`--publish` serves one partner and then exits, and `Ctrl+C` or `SIGTERM` stops
a waiting or serving `listen` cleanly with exit 0. Run terminal A first, then
paste its printed locator (the peer's dialable `ocapn://` address) into `LOC`
in terminal B. `init` mints the identity keys a peer signs its sessions with,
stored under `PANCAKE_STATE`; each terminal gets its own directory so it acts
as its own peer.

```sh
# terminal A
export PANCAKE_STATE=/tmp/pancake-a
pancake --json init
pancake --json ocapn listen --publish greeter
# {"ok":true,"locator":"ocapn://127.0.0.1%3A46659.tcp"}   (%3A is the : of host:port, URI-encoded)

# terminal B
export PANCAKE_STATE=/tmp/pancake-b
pancake --json init
LOC='ocapn://127.0.0.1%3A46659.tcp'   # paste A's locator
pancake --json ocapn call "$LOC" greeter greet world
#                         name──┘       │     └─ arg
#                         verb──────────┘
# {"ok":true,"value":"Hello, world"}
```

# REPL, MCP, and completion

The binary also serves CapTP tools over MCP and completes your shell. `pancake repl`
opens an interactive CapTP lab on a live session: the exports, imports, and
answers appear beside the prompt as you type the verbs, and typing `guide`
turns on a staged walkthrough. The REPL and `probe` want a live listener, so
their full recipes are in the [CLI guide](https://github.com/jimisaacs/pancake/blob/main/docs/cli.md).

```sh
pancake mcp --tools default                # CapTP tools for an editor assistant (MCP)
eval "$(pancake completion bash)"          # tab completion
```

For the library API behind these commands, continue to [Start
building]($link.page('start')). The [demo apps]($link.page('examples')) use the
same operations in a chat room, a task board, and a capability-oriented tool
service across five languages.
